on). Overall good but interpersonal and memory issues.\n\nCandidate C: strengths: makes correct decisions quickly (decision-making), keeps calm in crisis (calm), understands complicated technology (technical). Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas (teamwork), egocentric (crew cooperation), not willing to further education (development). Overall strong technical but poor teamwork.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately (decision-making), concentrates very well (cognitive), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (reliability). Weaknesses: know-it-all (could affect crew), hot temper (under pressure). So strong technical but interpersonal issues.\n\nWe need to pick provisional preference. Which candidate balances strengths and weaknesses best? Long-distance flights require calm, decision-making, technical competence, teamwork. Candidate A has strong leadership but show-off and not open to new ideas may hinder crew. Candidate B has good stress handling and conscientiousness but nasty remarks and weak number memory could be problematic. Candidate C is calm and quick decisions but poor communication and egocentric. Candidate D is problem solver and responsible but hot temper and know-it-all.\n\nWhich seems best? Possibly Candidate A: strong anticipation, spatial vision, leadership, but need to consider show-off and closed to new ideas. Could be mitigated? But we cannot mitigate; we must weigh. Candidate B's nasty remarks could be severe for crew. Candidate C's egocentric and communication issues also severe. Candidate D's hot temper could be dangerous under stress.\n\nThus Candidate A seems best overall despite interpersonal flaws. I will state provisional preference for Candidate A, with moderate confidence, noting uncertainties about interpersonal issues and openness to new ideas. Also note that more info on how show-off manifests would help.\n\nNow produce output."}
